{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/621918-the-doctor-as-an-unchained-cipher","id":621918,"title":"The Doctor As An Unchained + Cipher","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-09T23:50:14-07:00","id":621918,"title":"The Doctor As An Unchained + Cipher","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Brave/Creative</span></span><br /> <b>Vice:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Fickle </span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Incarnation:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Psychopomp</span></span><br /> <b>Agenda:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Inquisitor/Tempter</span></span><br /> <b>Catalyst:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Freedom Of Movement</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Intelligence 6, Wits 4, Resolve 5</span></span><br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4</span></span><br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Presence 4, Manipulation 5, Composure 4</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Academics (History) 4, Crafts (Machines) 6, Computer 4, Medicine 3, Occult 4, Politics 2, Investigation 4, Science (Time Travel) 6</span></span><br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Athletics (Running) 3, Brawl 1, Drive (TARDIS) 3, Firearms 2, Larceny (Sonic Screwdriver) 3, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Weaponry (Swords) 3</span></span><br /> <b>Social Skills:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Animal Ken 2, Empathy 3, Expression (Humor) 4, Intimidation (Grandiose Threats) 3, Persuasion (Leadership, Diplomacy) 4, Socialize 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge (Technobabble, Bluff) 3</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">Area Of Expertise (Time Travel, Sonic Screwdriver), Common Sense, Danger Sense, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics, Crafts, Science), Eye For The Strange, Fast Reflexes 2, Good Time Management, Indomitable (<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\">Epic</a></b>), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Time Travel, Sonic Screwdriver), Investigative Aide (Academics, Crafts, Science), Patient, Professional Training 5 (Time Lord: </span>Science, Expression, Persuasion), Tolerance For Biology, Trained Observer 3, Virtuous (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=847629#post847629\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>),<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Fleet Of Foot 3, Hardy 3, Greyhound, Iron Stamina 3, Parkour 4, Quick Draw (Sonic Screwdriver), Seizing The Edge, Sleight Of Hand, Closed Book 3, Contacts (Inquisitors, Tempters), Fast-Talking 4, Inspiring <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=1088037#post1088037\"><b>(Epic)</b></a>, </span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Iron Will, Pusher, Sympathetic, Table Turner, True Friend (Companions), </span></span>Untouchable, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration/page2\"><b>Untouchable Style 4</b></a>,<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Advance Form, Consummate Professional (Inquisitor, Tempter), Gadget (Sonic Screwdriver, Psychic Paper), Living The Lie, Multiple Agendas, Resonance Sensitive, Resonance Aware 3, TARDIS*, Terrible Form 4, Versatile Transformation</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Sonic Screwdriver's Embeds (Lambda):</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Open Sesame, Right Tools Right Job, Like I Built It and Cause And Effect.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Paper's Embed (Precision Engineered):</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Authorized.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>*</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The </span></span><b>TARDIS</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> is considered to be a Lare (see Demon's ST Guide Page 79) of Rank 5 with a special Incept, Influence or Numen that allows it to travel through space-time. It cannot travel to alternate planes of existence (use Rip The Gates for that). Its other traits are up to the ST.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Embeds</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Vocal:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Across A Crowded Room, Animal Communication, Borrowed Expertise, Eavesdrop, Everybody Knows, Imagine, Muse, Remote Link-Up, Voice Of The Machine</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Instrumental:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Data Retrieval, Efficiency, Functional Identity, Like I Built It, Open Sesame, Right Tools Right Job, Shift Consequence, Synthesis, Turn Blade</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Cacophony:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Bystander Effect, Cause And Effect, Cool Heads Prevail, Hesitation, Just Bruised, On The Mend, Raw Materials, Shatter, Special Someone</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mundane:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Associate And Integrate, Authorized, Deep Cover, Going Native, Homogeneous Memory, In My Pocket, Interference, Never Here, Occam's Razor, Persistent Legend, Quick Change, Without A Trace</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Exploits</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Allies Into Gold, Context Matters, Deep Pockets, Force Relationship, Four Minutes Ago, Hellhounds*, Inflict Stigmata, Rip The Gates, Stop<br /> <br /> *Uses Crafts instead of Animal Ken, since the Doctor builds his Cryptids from scratch as machines rather than transforming animals. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Demonic Form</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Modifications:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Blade Hand, Component Indicators, Sense The Angelic, Tough As Stone</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Technologies:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Aura Sight, Environmental Resistance, Mind Reading, Multiversal Antennae</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Propulsions:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Long Limbs, Plasma Drive</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Processes:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Amorphous, Memory Theft, Nanobot Composition</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> 7</span></span><br /> <b>Initiative:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> 10</span></span><br /> <b>Speed: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">15</span></span><br /> <b>Willpower:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> 9</span></span><br /> <b>Health:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> 9</span></span><br /> <b>Primum:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> 7</span></span><br /> <b>Glitches:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> The Doctor possesses two hearts that beat at an average of 170 times per minute, which is much faster than the 60 to 100 beats per minute of a human. This may be noticed through x-rays, stethoscopes or just by hand. Supernaturals with keen senses, such as vampires and werewolves, do not notice this from a distance like they normally would. This Glitch is a Major Brand.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Cipher </b></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Wibbly Wobbly, Timey Wimey</b><br /> <br /> Not even the Doctor knows every single quantum branch and cosmic permutation of all timelines, but he\u2019s been through enough to know the most important patterns to look out for in case he needs to make emergency alterations.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Cool Heads Prevail</i> and <i>Synthesis</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Academics + History Specialty + Time Travel Specialty With Area Of Expertise<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Doctor suffers a -3 penalty to all Mental rolls for the rest of the scene from the overload of information from all the timelines coursing through his mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The Doctor may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Doctor gains the Informed Condition, which he may apply to any roll that benefits from his Time Travel Specialty.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Doctor figures out how to piece it all together in the most efficient manner possible. He may designate a number of rolls equal to Primum to receive the Rote Quality, as long as they would benefit from his Time Travel Specialty. If any of these rolls would already have Rote Quality, he gains the Steadfast Condition instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Reverse The Polarity Of Neutron Flow</b><br /> <br /> The Doctor possesses such vast knowledge of occult physics that it often sounds like gibberish to most, but he use that knowledge to practical effect at a moment\u2019s notice, especially when lives are at stake.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Synthesis</i> and <i>Cause And Effect</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Science + Time Travel Specialty With Area Of Expertise<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Doctor Resolves the Informed Condition, but his Plan suffers from the Volatile Condition and offers half of its normal bonus round down. The Gadgets also suffer from the Volatile Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The Doctor may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Doctor can Resolve the Informed Condition to craft a Plan as an instant action. Add his Primum to the Wits + Composure dice pool for creating this Plan, and add the benefit of Resolving the Informed Condition to the roll. Alternatively, he may Resolve the Informed Condition to create a number of Gadgets up to Primum, which last for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Doctor prepares an additional number of Plans equal to his Primum/2 round up, and may select one Gadget to last for a full chapter.<br /> <br /> <b>Time Lord Victorious</b><br /> <br /> The Doctor may hesitate to use the full extent of his power for fear of the damage it may cause, but if the need is dire, he can put that hesitation aside and work both wonders and terrors.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Cause And Effect</i> and <i>Shift Consequence</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Occult + Time Travel Specialty With Area Of Expertise - Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> X Aether + 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Doctor must roll for Compromise at a -4 penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> No effect. The Doctor may try again, suffering a cumulative -1 for each new attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Once per chapter, by completing a Plan created with the previous Interlock, the Doctor may change a number up to Primum of targets of Conditions and/or Tilts affecting persons or locations encountered within the same Chapter. Each change costs 1 Aether.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Doctor gains the Steadfast Condition.</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-28-2017, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T03:48:31-07:00","id":622013,"title":"","content":"I'd charge more than 11 merit dots for the TARDIS as presented here; the travel ability is worth at least 3 on it's own. That said it is a very good description. Certainly beats your old Bygone interpretation. Thank you for sharing!<br /> <br /> As far as the Cipher goes, I like it for the most part. I don't like <i>The Adventure Continues' </i>s effect though I agree it is thematically appropriate. It just seems so...inelegant and heavy-handed. It could even to be argued that it undermines the 'natural' connections and relationships that develop during the adventures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T04:10:38-07:00","id":622042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/621918-the-doctor-as-an-unchained-cipher?p=622013#post622013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd charge more than 11 merit dots for the TARDIS as presented here; the travel ability is worth at least 3 on it's own. That said it is a very good description. Certainly beats your old Bygone interpretation. Thank you for sharing!<br /> <br /> As far as the Cipher goes, I like it for the most part. I don't like <i>The Adventure Continues' </i>s effect though I agree it is thematically appropriate. It just seems so...inelegant and heavy-handed. It could even to be argued that it undermines the 'natural' connections and relationships that develop during the adventures.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed, and edited accordingly. The Bolthole part of the TARDIS now explicitly has the Space-Time Travel (5) and Bigger On The Inside (4) advantages, which increase the dot rating of the Bolthole part from 6 to 15. Combined with the Subborned Infrastructure (5) part, the TARDIS is worth 20 Merit Dots. Could you please take another look at the 3 Interlocks? I think the Cipher is more mechanically elegant and thematically fitting now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-14-2015, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:37:31-07:00","id":622607,"title":"","content":"I decided to change the fourth Key from Fractal Reality to Imagine. The former is more about repetition, while the latter is about innovation. Besides, giving a Cipher with only Cacophony Embeds to the Doctor sounded weird to me.<br /> <br /> In the show, the Sonic Screwdriver has done dozens of things, but the Gadget version is more limited. The Unchained Doctor has the Efficient Hardware Merit at 4 dots, which allowed him to make a Sonic Screwdriver with Right Tools Right Job, Open Sesame, Data Retrieval and Shatter. He got an Exceptional Success on the Installation, so those 4 Embeds can be more callibrated and precise.<br /> <br /> The Gadget version of the Psychic Paper only has Authorized, but the Doctor got an Exceptional Success on that Installation as well. That lets the Psychic Paper fool both people and scanning technology.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I found 3 very good images that give an accurate idea of what the Doctor's Demonic Form looks like. Here are the <a href=\"http://gottagofeast.deviantart.com/art/LMS-HEX-178886965\" target=\"_blank\"><b>first</b></a>, the <b><a href=\"http://min.us/i/feRuR9ik3b9s\" target=\"_blank\">second</a>, </b>and the <a href=\"http://i45.photobucket.com/albums/f85/Moochava/etchedoraclesby343guiltwu3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>third.</b></a> The major difference is that his head is not featureless. It is still mechanical, but very human-like and expressive. <a href=\"http://th09.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2010/228/8/1/DW_Symbols_1___Time_Lord_by_DanYeomans.png\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Gallifreyan symbols</b></a> appear on his hands. His eyes just barely hold back the roaring storm of maniacal possibility and fractal blueprints just behind them, like a Genius with very high Inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-10-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:26:46-07:00","id":622719,"title":"","content":"I like the Condition-giving Interlocks, and the bonuses to teamwork actions. That's on-point. Not so sure about bonuses only when fixing the timeline, the Doctor changes things all the time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Those four Embeds do a pretty good job of modelling the Sonic Screwdriver. It's pretty counter to Demon as written (that's a... zeroth order lambda, right there!) but it's a simple solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T21:21:18-07:00","id":623091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/621918-the-doctor-as-an-unchained-cipher?p=622719#post622719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Condition-giving Interlocks, and the bonuses to teamwork actions. That's on-point. Not so sure about bonuses only when fixing the timeline, the Doctor changes things all the time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Those four Embeds do a pretty good job of modelling the Sonic Screwdriver. It's pretty counter to Demon as written (that's a... zeroth order lambda, right there!) but it's a simple solution.</div> </div> </div> </div> I partially agree. This Cipher is meant for large scale operations. Less important changes to the characters' lives are handled through narration, rather than rolls. He can use the Cipher to willingly change the timeline in a major way, but this is portrayed as a <b>Really Big Deal</b> in the show. To make that explicit, I added a disclaimer below the spoilered Cipher and slightly altered the phrasing for the Success of the third Interlock.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you liked the Sonic Screwdriver. You don't have to make the Efficient Hardware Merit universally available for Demons who meet the Prerequisites, of course. That would make the Doctor's Embedded Gadgets less impressive and likely cause plot holes in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-11-2015, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T02:02:02-07:00","id":643891,"title":"","content":"I like the revised Cipher.<br /> <br /> The Sonic works, though honestly I'd rather have it provide a bonus to using those Embeds than as a Gadget in it's own right (making it more about the Doctor doing stuff, than what the Screwdriver can do). But that is a personal preference and requires just as much homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T19:56:18-07:00","id":648527,"title":"","content":"I added the Sympathetic, Pusher, Taste and Patient Merits. I also added the Machines Specialty to his Areas Of Expertise. I added the two hearts of Time Lords as one of the Doctor's permanent Glitches caused by high Primum. Added the Eavesdrop, Muse, Across A Crowded Room, Animal Communication and Turn Blade Embeds. I changed the Data Retrieval Embed inside the Sonic Screwdriver into Like I Built It, and altered several Demonic Form powers. Added the Allies Into Gold and Demon House Exploits, with the latter applying to the TARDIS.<br /> <br /> As for K9, I'd say he is an intelligent Gadget, rather than a preexisting animal mutated through the Hellhound Exploit. The Doctor uses Embeds like Occam's Razor to make people think K9 is a hi-tech toy, science project and the like. K9 has been Embedded with Read Hostility, Right Tools Right Job, Remote Link-Up and Hesitation with the use of the Doctor's Efficient Hardware Merit. The first three Embeds allow him to sense incoming attacks to warn others, make the most of his built-in tools and establish remote communication with his friends, respectively. The last Embed fires laser beams, which can inflict the Stunned Tilt. Also, I like to imagine this version of K9 as looking like <a href=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20120217142929/tardis/images/9/9b/NewK9Mk2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this</b></a>, and having legs and retractable mini-arms for handling objects like a human. I suspect K9 didn't have legs in the show because of budget and special effects restrictions.<br /> <br /> Have some stats for a non-specific K9. I do know that intelligent Gadgets are not canon, but hey, Demons can already do all sorts of crazy stuff. A robot doggy Gadget doesn't sound like a stretch of the imagination to me.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Helpful<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Pedantic<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Chess) 3, Computer 3, Crafts 3, Investigation 3, Occult 3, Medicine 2, Science (Logic) 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Running) 3, Brawl (Bite) 2, Drive 1, Firearms (Lasers) 3, Larceny 1, Stealth 2, Weaponry 0<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 3, Expression 2, Intimidation 1, Persuasion (Being Cute) 3, Socialize (Friendly) 3, Streetwise 0, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Chess, Logic), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics, Science, Crafts), Eidetic Memory, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Logic, Being Cute, Friendly), Trained Observer 1, Indomitable, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Patient, Common Sense, Ambidextrous, Fleet Of Foot 2, Iron Stamina 2, Fast Reflexes 2, Quick Draw (Lasers), Sympathetic, Striking Looks +1 (Cute), True Friend (Companions, Doctor), Resonance Aware 3, Ambient Aether, Aether Pool<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed: </b>15<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Durability:</b> 3<br /> <b>Structure:</b> 7","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-01-2015, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:04:50-07:00","id":655977,"title":"","content":"Have some stats for a Cryptid version of the Weeping Angels. I cribbed some numbers and the Blink ability from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-the-nwod?p=402342#post402342\"><b>Eremite's Pandoran write-up</b></a>, because I thought they were fitting.<br /> <br /> <b>Original Species:</b> Bats (Size 1)<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 2, Wits 6, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 3, Dexterity 6, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Investigation (Searching) 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics (Flight) 3, Brawl (Bite) 3, Stealth (Hiding In Plain Sight) 4, Survival 2<br /> <b>Social Skills: </b>Empathy (Prey) 2, Intimidation 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Direction Sense, Patient, Tolerance For Biology, Ambidextrous, Demolisher 3, Iron Stamina 3, Telepathy 5<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower: </b>6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>9<br /> <b>Defense: </b>6 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Speed: </b>13 (20 In Flight)<br /> <b>Health: </b>8<br /> <br /> <b>Adaptations: </b>Aether Eater, Aether Hive, Alternate Composition (Stone: 5/3 Armor), Piecemeal Anatomy (Arms: +2 Grappling), Variable Form<br /> <br /> <b>Rank: </b>4<br /> <b>Max Aether/Per Turn: </b>20/4<br /> <br /> <b>Special Ability \u2013 Blink:</b> The Cryptid versions of the Weeping Angels behave like Pandorans when seen by mortals. They roll Resolve + Composure and Failure means they turn into stone, with the same modifiers used by Pandorans. They receive a bonus to this roll equal to the highest Primum of a present Demon, rather than the highest Azoth of a present Promethean. They may reanimate as a reflexive action when they are not being looked at, provided they have Aether in their system.<br /> <br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <br /> Bite \u2013 Dice Pool 7, +1L (Requires Grapple And Steals 1 Aether Per Successful Attack)<br /> Claws \u2013 Dice Pool 6, +0L","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-08-2015, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}